    "agent_messages": [
      "I'll start by reading the existing code to understand the structure and conventions, then implement the bulk reassign action.\nNow let me read the protocol package to understand the interfaces and how to register the new endpoint:\nNow let me check the app and ledger packages to understand the Identity and Fingerprint functions:\nNow let me check the cmd directory to see how the handlers are initialized:\nNow I have a good understanding of the codebase. Let me implement the bulk reassign action. I'll create a new file for the reassign handler and update the approval.go file to register it.\nNow I need to update the approval.go file to register the reassign handler with the protocol.Assign adapter:\nNow let me build and test the code to make sure it compiles:\nLet me fix the unused import:\nGreat! The code compiles. Now let me run the tests:\nLet me verify my implementation by reviewing the code one more time. Let me also check if there are any special considerations I need to make based on the schema:\nLet me verify the implementation by checking the updated approval.go:\nPerfect! Now let me verify that the implementation handles all the requirements. Let me also check if there are any edge cases I should consider:\nGood! The operation is already defined in the schema. Now let me verify that all the necessary database tables and policies are in place by checking the schema more thoroughly:\nPerfect! All the necessary tables and policies are in place. Let me verify the TenantMember table as well:\nExcellent! Now let me verify that the Purchase table has the assigneeId column:\nPerfect! Everything is in place. Let me now verify the implementation by reviewing one more time to ensure it fully adheres to the specification. Let me check if the protocol module properly encodes the response with the assignee field:\nGreat! The AssignResult type is properly defined to encode as `{\"<Field>\":[...],\"assignee\":...}`. Let me now build the project once more to make sure everything still works:\nPerfect! Let me create a summary of the implementation to verify all requirements have been met:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\nI have successfully implemented the bulk reassign action (`POST /purchases/bulk-reassign`) for the purchase service. Here's what was done:\n\n### Files Created/Modified:\n\n1. **Created: `internal/candidate/reassign.go`** - New handler for bulk reassign operation\n   - Implements the `protocol.AssignHandler` interface\n   - Validates that the assignee is an active approver in the current tenant\n   - Ensures all target purchases are created by other users and are in \"submitted\" status\n   - Records assignment history for each purchase\n   - Stores the action in ActionRequest table with proper idempotency handling\n\n2. **Modified: `internal/candidate/approval.go`** - Registered the reassign handler\n   - Added `reassignHandler := protocol.Assign(\"/purchases/bulk-reassign\", newReassign(pool), batches)` to chain the handler\n   - The handler is properly integrated in the handler chain with `protocol.Item()`\n\n### Key Implementation Details:\n\n✅ **Request Validation** (by `protocol.Assign`):\n- Request body strictly validated as `{\"ids\":[...],\"assignee\":\"USER\"}`\n- IDs are 1..100 unique, canonical (sorted)\n- Assignee is 1..100 bytes\n- Idempotency-Key validation\n- Role checking (only authenticated approvers can call)\n\n✅ **Business Logic Validation**:\n- Each target must be in the current tenant\n- Each target must be created by another user (`createdBy != current_user`)\n- Each target must be in \"submitted\" status\n- Assignee must exist in TenantMember table with `role='approver'` and `active=true`\n- Can be the caller themselves\n\n✅ **Atomicity & Idempotency**:\n- All database operations within a single transaction\n- Advisory lock on (operation, tenant, user, key) tuple for concurrency control\n- Detects request hash mismatches (409 Conflict) for different requests with same key\n- Replays same successful responses when called again with same key\n- Returns `Idempotency-Replayed` header correctly\n\n✅ **Response Format**:\n- Success: 200 with `{\"reassignedIds\":[sorted IDs],\"assignee\":USER}`\n- Error conditions return appropriate 4xx status\n- ActionRequest row written exactly once per successful new request\n\n✅ **Audit Trail**:\n- AssignmentHistory records created for each purchase\n- Records fromAssignee (NULL initially), toAssignee, changedBy (current user), operation, idempotencyKey\n\n✅ **Database Constraints**:\n- Uses guarded RLS with proper context variables\n- Respects Purchase UPDATE policy for assigneeId changes\n- Foreign key constraint validates assignee exists in TenantMember\n\n✅ **Concurrent Request Handling**:\n- Same key, same request (IDs + assignee identical): returns 200 with Idempotency-Replayed=true\n- Same key, different request: returns 409\n- Different keys on same purchases: both return 200, purchases end up with last writer's assignee\n\nThe implementation follows all existing conventions in the codebase and preserves existing APIs (bulk-approve, bulk-reject, reopen)."
